<title>USA: PORTFOLIO MANAGER OF TWO JANUS FUNDS QUITS - NYT.</title>
<headline>PORTFOLIO MANAGER OF TWO JANUS FUNDS QUITS - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The portfolio manager of two top-performing mutual funds of the Janus Funds abruptly quit his job, the New York Times reported.</p>
<p>Thomas Marsico had managed the $5.3 billion Janus Twenty fund and the $1.5 billion Janus Growth and Income fund, the paper said.</p>
<p>He resigned over &quot;philospohical differences&quot; with the company, a Janus spokeswoman told the paper.</p>
